Context
  Asked to make sure a PR checks frontmatter, evals and so on BEFORE release:start
  lands, and to consider stacking the deployable branches into one consolidated
  deployment.

  This branch is the first half. It is deliberately non-deployable -- tests/,
  Makefile and .github/ are not in SHIPPED -- so it can merge without publishing
  and without waiting on the release chain.

Deviations
  The reordering in gate.yml iterates over validator files rather than calling
  make targets. Calling `gmake check-monitors' here would break, because that
  target and its validator live on feat/monitor-repl-health; the loop tolerates a
  missing file, so gate.yml does not have to be edited again when that lands, and
  the two branches do not conflict on this file.

Considerations
  The test-port bug was found by my own carelessness and is worth recording as
  such: I piped `gmake checks' through tail, did not gate the commit on its exit
  status, and pushed feat/guile-project-scaffold on a 6-passed-1-failed run. The
  commit in this branch now gates on the exit code explicitly. The underlying flake
  is real and is fixed here; the process failure was mine.

  Frontmatter rules are judgement calls encoded as thresholds. The 80-character
  floor on description and the "Use when" clause requirement would both reject a
  terse but legitimate skill. They pass all three skills here, and the reasoning is
  in the validator's docstring, but they are conventions rather than spec.

Timeline
  2026-09-29, nexus, FreeBSD 15.1-RELEASE, guile3 3.0.10, as dsp-dr. Eight planted
  frontmatter faults, all caught. Concurrent two-worktree test run verified.
